Package: safepaste
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Alexei Migoun <alexei.migoun@ox.security>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11),
 python3-gi (>= 3.48),
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.14),
 gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5),
 python3-xlib (>= 0.33),
 python3-regex (>= 0.1.20221031),
 wl-clipboard (>= 2.2),
 libglib2.0-bin (>= 2.80)
Description: clipboard secret-guard for the Linux desktop
 SafePaste watches the desktop clipboard for credentials, API keys,
 tokens, private keys and other secrets, and keeps them off the clipboard
 by default rather than merely warning about them.
 .
 In the default "redact" mode, the instant a matching secret is copied
 the clipboard is replaced with a placeholder immediately -- only
 afterwards is a notification/dialog shown, offering to restore the
 original for a short window. That ordering is deliberate: ignoring the
 dialog, the dialog failing to appear, or the daemon dying mid-decision
 all still leave the clipboard safe, because the swap already happened.
 .
 Detection runs entirely on this machine against a vendored Gitleaks rule
 set plus a small number of SafePaste-specific rules; no network calls
 are made at runtime. The package installs a per-user background daemon
 (started automatically via a systemd user unit), an optional
 StatusNotifierItem tray icon, a Ctrl+Alt+V on-demand "sanitise now"
 shortcut, a D-Bus API for future integrations, and a `safepaste`
 command-line tool (scan/redact/rules/hash) for use outside the GUI.
 .
 Built and tested for Ubuntu 24.04 (GNOME 46, Wayland).
